WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.528
Welcome to our Understand Shipping Templates training.

00:00:02.528 --> 00:00:08.306
In this video, you'll learn about what shipping templates are, how to configure your shipping templates,

00:00:08.306 --> 00:00:13.000
how to set different shipping rate models, and how to offer free shipping.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.923
By the end of the video, you'll know how to fill out a shipping template and set more accurate customer

00:00:19.923 --> 00:00:22.000
delivery promises using Shipping Settings Automation.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Shipping templates enables you to customize options and then assign multiple ASINs to each template.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.529
Within a shipping template, you can configure transit times and fees for both domestic and international

00:00:36.529 --> 00:00:37.000
deliveries.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.000
You can create up to 20 shipping templates to have different shipping options for groups of SKUs.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Domestically, you can assign specific fees within a region of a country.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.545
Additionally, you can configure an option for customers to get expedited shipping and set a specific

00:00:53.545 --> 00:00:56.000
price for this accelerated transit time.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
From Seller Central, click the gear icon to open the Settings menu and then Shipping Settings.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:08.000
On the Shipping Settings page, you'll see two tabs, General Shipping Settings and Shipping Templates.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.875
By clicking the Shipping Templates tab, you can review existing templates, create new shipping templates,

00:01:14.875 --> 00:01:19.000
assign SKUs to templates, or edit any existing templates.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.000
To edit an existing template, click Edit Template.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:29.476
From here, you can choose a rate model and your shipping options, such as free economy, standard

00:01:29.476 --> 00:01:31.000
shipping, and expedited shipping.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.000
You can also take a tour of your Shipping Settings page by clicking Take the Tour.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:42.000
Make sure to check out our help pages on how to create new or edit existing shipping templates.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:47.000
Additional help pages can help you with weekend carrier operations and holiday settings.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.913
When setting shipping fees on your shipping template, you have two rate models to choose from, per

00:01:52.913 --> 00:01:55.000
item weight-based and price-banded.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.938
If you select per item weight-based, you can select a shipping fee for each item shipped, plus a

00:02:00.938 --> 00:02:05.000
shipping fee for each additional item or pound that the first item weighs.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.452
It's important to note that if you set your fee to $0, your customers will see a banner that says

00:02:11.452 --> 00:02:15.000
Free Shipping, which typically leads to more product views and sales.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:21.667
If you select price-banded, you can select a shipping fee for ASINs up to a specific limit and then

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:25.000
assign a different shipping fee for anything above that limit.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.000
Additionally, if you're shipping in the US, you'll see a section called Free Economy.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.000
This section offers customers the option to select a slower delivery promise that has free shipping.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:42.800
But if you want to make free shipping your main customer delivery promise, set your standard shipping

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.000
fee to $0.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.000
On your shipping templates, you can configure the transit time for your customer delivery promise.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:56.107
You can manually estimate the transit time to each region and use the drop-down menu to assign the

00:02:56.107 --> 00:02:59.000
number of days your products will take to arrive.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.684
If you also want to learn more about the customer delivery promise, check out our video on shipping

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.000
settings.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:11.000
Keep in mind that setting a longer transit time may cause your offer to look less appealing to customers.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:16.000
We often find that sellers overestimate how long shipping takes.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:22.364
You can also enable shipping settings automation, or SSA, to provide an automated calculation based

00:03:22.364 --> 00:03:29.152
on your warehouse location, the location of the customer, and the carriers and ships that method

00:03:29.152 --> 00:03:30.000
you use.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.000
If you want to learn more about SSA, check out our shipping settings automation video.

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:41.522
In addition to your standard delivery promise, you can offer customers a faster delivery alternative

00:03:41.522 --> 00:03:45.000
by enabling expedited shipping on your shipping template.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:51.750
By doing so, you can configure a specific shipping fee to expedite the delivery, as well as which

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.000
regions you offer this service in.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:04:00.222
Additionally, if you meet the requirements to offer premium shipping, you can enable one or two-

00:04:00.222 --> 00:04:01.000
day delivery.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:07.111
It's important to note that these customer delivery promises include same-day handling time for

00:04:07.111 --> 00:04:09.148
orders received before 2 p.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:09.556
m.

00:04:09.556 --> 00:04:12.000
local time, plus the transit time.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:18.286
For this reason, you must ensure your business can meet this turnaround time before enabling premium

00:04:18.286 --> 00:04:23.000
shipping and selecting the regions where you want to offer these options.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:29.400
After watching this video, you should now know what shipping templates are, how to navigate shipping

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:37.000
templates, how to set your shipping fees per item or by price band, and how to offer free shipping.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:43.800
Make sure to return to the shipping settings page to review and update your shipping settings or

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.000
templates as needed.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:48.500
This concludes our training on shipping templates.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:51.167
Thank you and happy selling in the Amazon store.
